items.test:
Commands that passed, with counts:
- npx vitest run test/unit/question-whole-text.test.ts: 3 tests. The Question carries the whole text for type_text and borrowed typing, shown as typed (⏎, ⟨RLO⟩); there is none for short text; fill_cells lists every cell whole.
- npx vitest run test/unit/confirm-whole-text.test.ts: 12 tests. Covered:
  - bubble.whole is {n,text,seen:false,page:0};
  - Allow from the button or the key is refused before and taken after wholeSeen;
  - wholeSeen for the wrong question is false;
  - 'Always' waits too;
  - the key adds one page per press, not while Ember drives the mouse;
  - Not now works at once;
  - short and empty text are unchanged;
  - wholeSeenOf and waitsForWhole;
  - the hint equals CONSENT_READ_HINT;
  - main's route order;
  - the eval user. Without the runner change the eval test times out: the answer is refused.
- npx vitest run packages/bubble/src/whole.test.ts: 8 tests. The block counts as in view only at its end or when it fits, on screen, in its typeface, hidden counting as not in view. It is armed and reported once. A new question starts unread. Pages per key press since the last state. The announcement and the CSS.

Scratch Electron runs of the built overlay and corner card (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Ember-Powered-by-Github-Copilot/9df81ff3-d6fa-5078-ac02-9c8dbaa6cb03/scratchpad/wholecheck/main.cjs and elsewhere.cjs, with screenshots alongside):
- 2 key pages reach the end and send ui:seen:1;
- scrolling half way sends nothing, the end sends ui:seen:2;
- a block that fits sends ui:seen:3 once drawn;
- on another display or with Ember hidden, nothing is sent;
- at the Larger text size, 3 pages reach the end;
- the corner card sends ui:seen:5 at its end;
- Allow's aria-disabled clears in each case.

test/unit/shortcut-fallback.test.ts (new, 28 tests). It was written before the code and failed first on the missing exports and module. It covers:
- the fallback table against canonicalKeys and isSystemKey on all 3 OSes;
- heldShortcuts;
- holdShortcuts with a fake globalShortcut: default free, default taken, both taken then retried, fallback kept once the default frees, question keys, a registry that throws;
- keyboardRoute;
- the setup check row per state and OS;
- keysLine per state;
- consent cards with fallback, none and default;
- runtime passing stopKey to all 6 cards;
- --ask, startView, the jump-list task (packaged and development), the Dock items;
- the .desktop groups, appimage.sh and the RPM wrapper;
- main.ts wiring, read from its source.

home-platform-copy.test.ts: new block of 3 tests (fallback in every sentence, none-held twins per OS, question keys), with the page-model selectors extended. The two none-held tests failed on the old page.

packaging.test.ts: the smoke stand-in now handles --ask (passing case and a new 'no-ask' failing case), plus a pin on the CI desktop-entry check.

Updated pins: environment-platforms, environment, main-held-keys, main-privacy-wiring.

Scratch repros on Xvfb with the real build (scripts in scratchpad/sc3-blocker/):
- An Electron 'blocker' holds Control+Alt+Space, Control+Alt+X and Control+Alt+Shift+X. Ember logs `shortcut.unavailable` with taken [those three], fallback ["ask"], missing ["stop"].
- Reading the real settings page over CDP: stop shows Ctrl+Alt+Shift+X, the :has selector hides the settings line and shows #settings-taken, and the ask none-twin is shown.
- An onboarded profile started with --ask opens the ask box (ask.open source launcher, ask.keyboard, no window.home.shown). A second --ask start logs instance.second {ask:true} and ask.open.
